        "kind": "web form",
        "value": "https://www.cornerstonecomfort.net/contact-cornerstone-comfort",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.cornerstonecomfort.net/contact-cornerstone-comfort"
      }
    ]
  },
  "discovery": {
    "questions": [
      "When a homeowner submits a quote request through your website or instant estimate tool, how quickly does that inquiry appear in Housecall Pro?",
      "Are your Google Ads and Meta campaign leads automatically tracked through to completed jobs and revenue in Housecall Pro, or do you reconcile ROI by hand?",
      "How does your team currently manage inbound customer emails across [redacted] and [redacted] during winter freezes and peak summer heatwaves?"
    ],
    "outreachSubject": "[redacted] - lead response & Housecall Pro sync at Cornerstone Comfort",
    "outreachBody": "Hi [redacted],\n\nI came across Cornerstone Comfort while looking at top-rated HVAC and water contractors in Nampa and the Treasure Valley. Congratulations on building a strong reputation with over 500 reviews since 2011.\n\nI noticed you are running paid search campaigns and offer an instant estimate feature on your website. When homeowners reach out online for heating or water heater quotes, getting those inquiries into Housecall Pro within two minutes and following up immediately often determines whether you book the job or they call another local contractor.\n\nAt ForgeX, we provide fixed-price automation that routes web quote requests directly into your field-service software and triggers instant customer confirmation so no lead gets lost. We also offer a $500 Revenue Leak Check that audits your inbound pipeline over one week to measure where quotes might be slipping through.\n\nWe do not make blanket revenue promises, but if you would like to see how other contractors eliminate lead lag between their website and dispatch board, I would welcome a brief 10-minute conversation.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Founder Name]\nForgeX\n[Founder Postal Address]\nTo stop receiving emails, please reply with 'unsubscribe'."
  },
